<header><p class="st-kicker">nomadic confederation · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Kutrigurs</h1><p class="st-meta">480 CE – 570 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Nomads of the steppe west of the Don whose raid under Zabergan in 559 reached the outskirts of Constantinople.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Kutrigurs are named by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/procopius">Procopius</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agathias">Agathias</a> in the 6th century as a Hunnic or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgar</a> people of the steppe between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/don-river">Don</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a>, kin to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/utigurs">Utigurs</a> to their east. They emerged from the remnants of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hunnic-empire">Hunnic Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oghurs">Oghur</a> peoples who arrived after 463.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>As pastoral nomads under chiefs, they lived on herding and raids into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>, sometimes serving <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a> and sometimes, as in 551, allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gepids">Gepids</a> against it. In 559 their khan Zabergan crossed the frozen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and threatened <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, until the aged general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius">Belisarius</a> repelled him. Justinian then turned the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/utigurs">Utigurs</a> against them.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Weakened by war with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/utigurs">Utigurs</a>, the Kutrigurs fell under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avars</a> in the 560s; many joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/avar-khaganate">Avar Khaganate</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pannonia">Pannonia</a>. Others later joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kubrat">Kubrat's</a> <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/old-great-bulgaria">Old Great Bulgaria</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="nomadic confederation, 480 CE – 570 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 74 V58 Q50 30 82 58 V74 Z"/><path d="M42 74 V60 H58 V74"/><path d="M30 50 L50 36 L70 50"/><path d="M50 36 V26"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">nomadic confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central Asia and the Steppe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:69.25%;width:1.79%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>480 CE – 570 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>nomadic confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Zabergan, Sinnion</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Tengrism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Oghur Turkic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, <a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kutrigur Huns, Cutrigurs</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=525&amp;focus=kutrigurs" aria-label="Kutrigurs on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5415 459 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kutrigurs lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5735 715h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5735 715h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Ukraine. <a href="/atlas?year=525&amp;focus=kutrigurs">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

